cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this formalization or build upon it,
  please cite this repository using the metadata below.
type: software
title: "The Conway–Soifer conjecture for n = 3: a Lean formalization"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kuznetsov"
    given-names: "Vladislav"
    affiliation: "Moscow Institute of Physics and Technology"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AnanasClassic/conway-soifer-n3-lean"
url: "https://github.com/AnanasClassic/conway-soifer-n3-lean"
abstract: >-
  A standalone, kernel-checked Lean 4 proof of the n = 3 case
  of the Conway–Soifer covering conjecture: for every epsilon > 0,
  an equilateral triangle of side 3 + epsilon cannot be covered
  by ten closed unit equilateral triangles, with arbitrary
  positions, rotations, and overlaps. Equivalently, ten congruent
  closed equilateral triangles covering an equilateral triangle
  of side 3 must have common side length at least 1.
  The formalization includes 100 certificates and 3188 forced
  point-to-owner assignments. The final theorems depend only on
  the standard axioms propext, Classical.choice, and Quot.sound.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - discrete geometry
  - covering problems
  - equilateral triangles
  - Conway–Soifer conjecture
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
